You know what I love about that statement?

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.390
It's such a small statement, OK?

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:42.390
It's so tiny.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:50.030
It's just a little sentence, two sentences,
I guess, technically, but it says so much.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:53.979
About American politics today, not just about
Trump, not just about the Republican Party,

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:56.829
but it says so much about politics.

00:01:56.829 --> 00:02:00.229
So I have to break this statement down again,
this tiny little statement.

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:02.979
I'm breaking it down three different ways.

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:11.050
The first one is take off partizan blinders,
get rid of hatred for Trump, get rid of support

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.160
for infrastructure, all of that.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:17.150
Let's just look at this as political strategy,
because what I'm going to say here might shock

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:21.610
you from a strategy standpoint.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.610
Trump is right.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:28.410
I know, I know it's weird to even say it,
but.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.209
He's right.

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:36.709
What's the Republican's best chance to win
in the twenty twenty two midterms, showing

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:41.590
the public that the Democrats couldn't get
anything done, showing the public that all

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:46.660
these lofty goals of the Democratic Party
fell flat?

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:50.290
And of course, by doing that, they're going
to omit the part where they're the ones who

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.320
made it all fail.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.590
That's how the talking point works.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:58.849
But Mitch McConnell was very clear a couple
months ago when he said on camera, we've got

00:02:58.849 --> 00:03:02.510
to make sure that they can't move forward
on their agenda because McConnell knows the

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.430
same thing.

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:10.220
They've got to make a pitch to voters because
so far all their attacks on Biden have failed.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.890
That's another important thing to remember,
folks.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.800
All their attacks have failed so far.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:22.620
Because they don't have anything real to attack
him on, so if they give him this infrastructure

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:26.680
package, that is a big win for the Democratic
Party.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:30.209
Not as big as it should have been, certainly
not as big as they were asking for in the

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:34.629
plan, but if the Democrats produce, if the
Democrats go to the public and say, we got

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:38.340
through this because remember, it's not just
an infrastructure plan, folks.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:45.780
It is a jobs plan that is widely supported
by members of both parties out there in America.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:54.230
So, again, this is only looking at this through
nonpartizan eyes, Trump saying, do not support

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.370
this.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:04:02.400
That is what the Republicans would be doing,
except, of course, the other side of that

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.849
strategy.

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:07.290
And this is where Trump is totally wrong on
it.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:11.720
As I just mentioned, majority of Republicans
out there support this hack, a majority of

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:17.570
Republicans even support raising taxes on
the wealthy and corporations to pay for it.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:21.040
They supported it before it was even cut down
to one point two trillion.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.630
They liked it when it was three and a half
trillion.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:26.520
They want the plan.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:31.790
So they would be less likely in turn based
on that, to believe Republican talking points

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:36.980
that Democrats were unable to deliver because
they're clearly paying at least somewhat attention

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.630
to this issue.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.290
And that's another positive development.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.880
They know who's holding this thing up.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.720
They know that they want it and they know
that Republicans and to a degree mansion and

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.170
cinema don't want them to have it.

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:57.070
So that's why Republicans are stuck between
the rock and a hard place here on terms of

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:05.530
strategy, they want to get Democrats to lose,
but they can't have their voters who support

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:10.900
this bill know that they were the ones who
kept it from making it to them.

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:16.280
So I think at this point, some of them clearly
not all of them, but I do think some of them

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:23.230
have looked at this and said, you know what,
the best path forward for us is probably to

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:29.130
let this thing happen, at least, hey, maybe
then if there are some positive developments

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:33.910
out of it, once it passes, I can go back to
my constituents and tell them I supported

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:34.910
this thing.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:35.910
I did this for you.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.730
I did this for you.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:43.970
So that could likely be the strategy that
these people take moving forward.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:51.300
And of course, there's also the third part,
and that is who cares if Trump withholds his

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.300
endorsement?

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:58.180
There was a study that came out last week
and I actually spoke about this on my other

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:01.040
channels because it's a phenomenal study and
I love it.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:06.290
They looked at races where Donald Trump endorsed
the candidate versus races where Donald Trump

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:12.410
did not endorse a candidate and the political
scientists who looked at all of these endorsements

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.260
and all of the outcomes.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:18.650
Came to a statistical conclusion.

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:22.730
That a Donald Trump endorsement.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:30.990
Makes you two and a half percent less likely
to win your race, candidates who received

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:35.500
the Trump endorsement again, two and a half
percent, not two and a half times, two and

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.620
a half percent.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:44.300
Less likely to win, so it's a very, very tiny,
tiny disadvantage, but it's a disadvantage

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.950
nonetheless.

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:51.750
And the report also did mention that know
when Trump endorses a candidate, they end

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.480
up raising a ton more money.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.100
But you know who else does?

00:06:56.100 --> 00:07:02.640
Their opponent, every time Trump comes out
and endorses somebody, they raise more money,

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:05.000
but so does their opponent.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:10.330
They also found that voter turnout actually
does increase in races where Donald Trump

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:11.750
endorses a candidate.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:20.090
But again, in most instances, it benefits
the opponent, not the person Trump endorsed.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:21.780
So Trump wants to be the kingmaker.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.920
He's out there pretending to be the kingmaker.

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:28.182
He's threatening them, trying to scare them
into submission, saying, I'm not going to

00:07:28.182 --> 00:07:30.080
endorse you if you don't do this.

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:35.330
And Republicans need to respond with respond
with good like please don't endorse me.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:38.090
In fact, could you endorse my primary opponent?

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.270
Because I really want to win this election.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:45.900
And your endorsement at this point is effectively
a kiss of death.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:50.900
You're not helping candidates, you're hurting
them, you're literally making things more

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:58.050
difficult for them, so don't come out there
acting like I'm going to withhold my endorsement.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:00.040
Don't threaten us with a good time, man.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.950
We have seen the numbers.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.440
We know what the data looks like.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:08.630
We know that your endorsement doesn't change
people's minds.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:13.450
And when it does, it changes them in favor
of the other candidate.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:20.630
So, again, Republicans, you're not actually
stuck between a rock and a hard place here.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:25.750
You've got a pretty easy out vote in favor
of the infrastructure package, go back to

00:08:25.750 --> 00:08:30.620
your constituents, tell them that you delivered
it for them, and give Donald Donald Trump

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:36.140
the finger on the way out the door, because
trust me, you don't want his endorsement unless,

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:39.440
of course, you're looking forward to early
retirement.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:45.280
That would really be the only thing that would
work in your favor at that point.

